{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For</b> — \"to justice shall judgment return.\" HaShem [acts] with universals; in particulars there are times when there is no justice. Now I shall give you a parable: when rain falls upon the earth, it is justice and kindness to the universal — all who need water; yet for the few, who are particulars, it is not justice, for the rain harms them in most cases. And the vav after it returns to justice. And the sense: though the wicked oppress you, they have not departed from justice but pursue after it — all the upright of heart, who are the people of YHWH in truth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:15.241089875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}